From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 04:10:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] net: stmmac: drop the rest of the frame when napi_build_skb() fails

If napi_build_skb() fails on the first buffer of a frame that spans
several descriptors, stmmac_rx() drops that buffer but goes on with the
next descriptor of the same frame as if a new frame started there. The
rest of the frame is then passed up the stack as a frame of its own.

Mark the frame as errored instead, so that its remaining descriptors are
discarded like those of a frame with a receive error. The frame is
counted once in rx_dropped and once against the NAPI budget.

7.3 backport: the poll also keeps the frame state when it stops at a
descriptor the DMA still owns, so the rest of a dropped frame is still
discarded in the next poll. Upstream does this since
commit 26219e9402c2 ("net: stmmac: take ownership of saved RX state at poll entry").

Fixes: ec222003bd94 ("net: stmmac: Prepare to add Split Header support")
Assisted-by: Claude
Signed-off-by: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
---
diff --git a/drivers/net/ethernet/stmicro/stmmac/stmmac_main.c b/drivers/net/ethernet/stmicro/stmmac/stmmac_main.c
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/stmicro/stmmac/stmmac_main.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/stmicro/stmmac/stmmac_main.c
@@ -5912,6 +5912,7 @@
 	unsigned int count = 0, error = 0, len = 0;
 	int status = 0, coe = priv->hw->rx_csum;
 	unsigned int next_entry = rx_q->cur_rx;
+	bool in_progress = false;
 	enum dma_data_direction dma_dir;
 	unsigned int desc_size;
 	struct sk_buff *skb = NULL;
@@ -5979,6 +5980,8 @@
 
 		prefetch(np);
 
+		in_progress = status & rx_not_ls;
+
 		if (priv->extend_desc)
 			stmmac_rx_extended_status(priv, &priv->xstats, rx_q->dma_erx + entry);
 		if (unlikely(status == discard_frame)) {
@@ -6098,7 +6101,7 @@
 							 buf->page);
 				buf->page = NULL;
 				rx_dropped++;
-				count++;
+				error = 1;
 				goto drain_data;
 			}
 
@@ -6129,8 +6132,10 @@
 drain_data:
 		if (likely(status & rx_not_ls))
 			goto read_again;
-		if (!skb)
+		if (!skb) {
+			count++;
 			continue;
+		}
 
 		/* Got entire packet into SKB. Finish it. */
 
@@ -6172,7 +6177,7 @@
 		count++;
 	}
 
-	if (status & rx_not_ls || skb) {
+	if (in_progress || skb) {
 		rx_q->state_saved = true;
 		rx_q->state.skb = skb;
 		rx_q->state.error = error;
-- 
